WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.176 --> 00:00:04.863
[Audio Description not captioned]

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:12.471
[Music]

00:00:12.471 --> 00:00:16.080
[Patricia Flatley Brennan, RN, PhD] NLM has&nbsp;
a 50-year history of conducting research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.051
here on the NIH campus. We call this&nbsp;
our Intramural Research Program.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:28.080
The research that we do uses mathematics and&nbsp;
computer science techniques to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.275
truth and clinical experiences&nbsp;
by looking at large data sets.

00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:39.948
[Valerie Florence, PhD] I believe that research&nbsp;
is the heart of the library and should be there.
&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.280
and we are the world's&nbsp;
library and we have research.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.640
It's important because it will advance the&nbsp;
approaches used in libraries all over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:59.920
world to manage and integrate and find&nbsp;
data so we can all get healthier faster.

00:01:04.418 --> 00:01:07.840
[Sameer Antani, Phd] There's always more research&nbsp;
to be done. I think we are the cusp at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:14.070
beginning of trying to understand human bodies&nbsp;
and the information that is contained in it.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.240
Each day, different parts of the NIH&nbsp;
are discovering new things. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:26.521
that presents NLM with an opportunity to keep&nbsp;
toe-to-toe so that the two can work together.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.960
[Brennan] Now, our Intramural Research&nbsp;
Program actually has two key components.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.280
In our Computational Biology branch,&nbsp;
investigators use bioinformatics tools&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.920
to understand the structure and function&nbsp;
of genes and other kinds of protein data.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.880
In our Computational Health Informatics&nbsp;
branch, our investigators are trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.600
to draw insights out of information&nbsp;
about the clinical process of patients

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.880
or the literature that describes clinical care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.409
What's exciting is that we've actually unified&nbsp;
these two programs under a single umbrella.

00:02:11.918 --> 00:02:19.120
[Florence] A really special thing is training&nbsp;
and mentoring a next generation of scientists.

00:02:23.668 --> 00:02:28.000
[Lauren Porter PhD] NLM has a really strong&nbsp;
track record in computation. There are a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.710
excellent scientists here and so I thought it&nbsp;
would be great to be able to work with them.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.440
And I'm really happy to be here and&nbsp;
be able to like take chances that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.564
I probably couldn't do in most other environments.

00:02:42.564 --> 00:02:45.584
[Antani] We have an&nbsp;
opportunity before us where ...

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:56.720
all our findings, once translated, would&nbsp;
reduce the barriers to access to medicine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:02.126
improve treatability, improve early detection&nbsp;
which leads to better quality of life.

00:03:02.126 --> 00:03:06.560
[Florence] Our whole goal is to&nbsp;
understand more about how living things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.787
work in order to improve the health of humans.

00:03:10.244 --> 00:03:16.975
[Music]

00:03:16.975 --> 00:03:19.229
[Music fades to silence]

